jstack includes material from these projects. This file is the record of what came from
where, with the exact commit; the skills themselves do not repeat it.

t3dotgg/tstack @ 1085050f3baed1ac724caa4a8166145fb2ac88af
  Skills: babysit-pr, file-pr, full-send, leaving-pr-comments, cross-review (adapted from its
  sol-loop; renamed). scripts/pr-wait is adapted: review bots are configurable instead of fixed.
  iterate draws on full-send ("ask only when you cannot continue alone", smallest change) and
  babysit-pr (keep the PR at the size the goal needs).

backnotprop/pstack @ 25abb38559ddbabec563646224d09eff9a250eca
  Mirror of cursor/plugins (pstack by Poteto). https://github.com/cursor/plugins
  Skills: prove-it (from principle-prove-it-works), correct-mistakes (from
  correct), create-verify (from create-verification-skill), fanout (adapted
  from swarm), iterate (adapted from figure-it-out, principle-attack-the-premise
  and principle-never-block-on-the-human).

michaelshimeles/rstack @ 11b15767d7587bab11f6c4957507b5f26d1785c7
  ticket-start is adapted from the steps of rstack's new-feature skill, and
  evidence from the protocol of its evidence-driven-testing skill.
  rstack publishes no root license for new-feature. No rstack files are copied.

cursor/plugins (pstack) @ 2776ddd2355d6d6c8747d3964600f28daf62f049
  Ideas and some wording adapted in 0.7.0: prove-it ("How sure are you" levels and the load-bearing
  fact, from its blast-radius skill; the two-edit test check, from principle-test-behavior-not-
  implementation), babysit-pr (treating review text as data and the red-CI triage, from its babysit
  playbook), full-send ("What blocks", from its autopilot-full playbook), cross-review verify mode and
  evidence/proof-valid (a verdict that only a non-author gives, and a proof that follows the patch id,
  from its shipping playbook), jstack/trail (an append-only decision log, from show-me-your-work).

1.0.0 folds the skills named above into fewer: ticket (from full-send, file-pr, ticket-start, prove-it,
evidence and iterate), review (from cross-review) and wave (from fanout, quota-gate and wrap-up). The credits
above apply to the text that moved. New in 1.0.0: the Evidence section of a pull request (a Before / After
table, "Not shown", "Who did the work") follows the pull requests of pingdotgg/t3code as read on 2026-11-14
(no text copied), and wave's "you run the program, not the code", fresh workers and accounting for every worker
follow the Orchestrate playbook of cursor/plugins (pstack) as ported in michael-denyer/pstack-claude @ a12b047.

